{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OSS consensus audit (2026-08-13): APPROVED pattern.\n\nSetuptools states that sdist/wheel artifacts are stable for a test round, builds them once under a session lock, and exposes session-scoped readonly fixtures (pypa/setuptools@7d53128, setuptools/tests/fixtures.py#L70-L130). PyPA Build likewise builds a dependency wheel once in a session fixture for downstream tests (pypa/build@bf222f4, tests/test_projectbuilder.py#L427-L438).\n\nThis ticket's boundary is equally conservative: share only immutable clean inputs and identical prerequisite artifacts inside one pytest session; retain distinct real wheel-from-sdist, empty-env failure, sdist-content, and rebuild-from-sdist executions. Tracker cross-check: ducal-statuelike-ladybird requires those real boundaries but does not require rebuilding identical prerequisites per assertion. No rejection found."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786638514902213001,"uuid":"21b6bdf7-3dbc-4d7d-b741-b8ed3d4f3edb"}